A copy of the parts of the C4-TT7's /sys that tt7d reads, taken from the real
panel's discovery dump (hardware/discovery/boot-0001-up22s: input-sysfs.txt,
backlight-sysfs.txt, power-supply-sysfs.txt, sys-class.txt, ip-link.txt).

Not from the dump: net/*/operstate is inferred from the UP/DOWN state in
ip-link.txt; sound/* and video4linux/* only list names in sys-class.txt, so
those directories hold an empty .keep file for git.

input/inputN/eventN (empty dirs) mirror the real sysfs layout: the dump's
input-devices.txt says Handlers=event0 for the keypad and event1 for gslX680.
